PLOT/UNPLOT ROUTINES - CORTEX BASIC REV. 1.1

             16  *
             17  *         PLOT AND UNPLOT POINT/LINE ROUTINES
             18  *
             19  *  FORMAT:
             20  *    PLOT  A,B             PLOT POINT (A,B)
             21  *    PLOT  TO A,B          PLOT LINE FROM CURSOR TO (A,B)
             22  *    PLOT  A,B TO C,D      PLOT LINE FROM (A,B) TO (C,D)
             23  *    UNPLOT A,B            UNPLOT POINT (A,B)
             24  *    UNPLOT TO A,B         UNPLOT LINE FROM CURSOR TO (A,B)
             25  *    UNPLOT A,B TO C,D     UNPLOT LINE FROM (A,B) TO (C,D)
             26  *
             27  *   FOLLOWING ONE OF THESE STATEMENTS THE CURSOR IS
             28  *   POSITIONED AT THE LAST CO-ORDINATE PAIR SPECIFIED.
             29  *
             30  *   AFTER THE LAST CO-ORDINATE PAIR A 'TO' MAY BE USED
             31  *   TO EXTEND THE LINE (UN)PLOTTING WITHIN THE ONE
             32  *   STATEMENT.  EG:-
             33  *
             34  *   PLOT TO A,B TO C,D TO E,F     THIS WILL PLOT THE 3 LINES
             35  *                                 1.  FROM CURSOR TO (A,B)
             36  *                                 2.  FROM (A,B) TO (C,D)
             37  *                                 3.  FROM (C,D) TO (E,F)
             38  *
             39  *
